Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?HTDESIGNER-45:=20=E9=A1=AF=E7=A4=BA=20Tab=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E9=A0=86=E5=BA=8F=20--=20the=20page's=20Tab=20stops=20numbered?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20and=20checked=20against=20the=20.dfm's=20TabOrder=20(0.45.0)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

BCB6's Edit > Tab Order / WinForms' View > Tab Order, read-only: every place
the page's Tab key stops gets a small badge, numbered in the page's real
Tab order (positive tabindex first, then the DOM; disabled / hidden / not
drawn ones skipped), compared with the order the .dfm gives the Tab key:
- blue "3": 3rd, as in the .dfm; red "3≠5": 3rd on the page, 5th in the
  .dfm (ranks among the controls both have); grey "·": the page stops there,
  the .dfm has no such stop (a TSpeedButton that became a <button> ...)
- lib/taborder.js: VCL's rule -- a container's windowed children by
  TabOrder, each followed by its own, depth first; TabStop (the .dfm's, else
  the class default); graphic controls, invisible / disabled ones and what
  is inside them left out; compareTabOrder
- right-click / palette toggle; the status bar says how many are out of
  order, the list goes to the output panel; the hint line explains colours

Tests: lib (HotPlate's real order; a made-up form for every rule and a
swapped pair), probe (the first two stops swapped in the given order -> red
1≠2 / 2≠1, 3 blue, the rest grey, the reply counts them, off = none), smoke
(the .dfm order to the probe, the reply reported), real VS Code (HotPlate:
13 stops, 8 in the .dfm, 0 out of order; badges drawn, off = none).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
